# Analysis: gardening-pathway prevalence by habitat type (Barcelona province)

## Inputs
- data/invaded_niche_pathways.csv - 632 plots x 37 cols. **TAB-separated despite .csv**. Plot = row; one habitat label per plot; 10 habitat types; no NA; n.gard+n.unint+n.agfo == n.total in 632/632 rows. 441/632 plots have n.total = 0.
- data/invasion_success_pathways.csv - 81 species x 19. Real CSV + CRLF. Only species-level traits; NO species x habitat matrix (only habitat.range breadth) -> context/mechanism only.
- data/temporal_trends_contingency_table.csv - 4 periods x 3 pathways (TAB). Background only.
- data/phylogenetic_tree.txt - NOT used: unit of analysis is the plot, not the species; no phylogenetically-independent contrast is needed for this question (and only 79/80 tip labels match).

## Code (run in order)
1. work/01_inspect.py - raw inventory (types, labels, NA, identity checks, duplicates).
2. work/02_diag.py - denominators, cross-table consistency, tree matching, covariate collinearity.
3. work/03_analysis.py - MAIN: two-layer descriptives, binomial GLM (10 habitat levels), omnibus LRT + 5000-permutation check, Holm pairwise (>=10 records rule), sensitivity analyses, ASCII forest plot.
4. work/04_extra.py - pathway composition per habitat, unconditional-layer pairwise (Holm), permutation omnibus for the unconditional layer.
5. work/05_jackknife_named.py - drop-one-plot jackknife of key contrasts.
Environment: python 3.12, pandas 3.0.2, statsmodels 0.14.6, scipy 1.16.0. matplotlib absent and not installable (no network) -> figure is ASCII.

## Model definitions
- Conditional layer: p_i = n.gard_i / n.total_i on the 191 plots with n.total>0; GLM cbind(n.gard, n.other) ~ C(habitat), binomial logit, reference level Urban (largest denominator). Levels with 0 or 100% prevalence flagged as separated.
- Unconditional layer: share of ALL plots in a habitat with n.gard>0 (denominator = all plots of that habitat).
- patsy has no cbind(), so models are fitted with sm.GLM on a 2-column endog (helper fitb()).
- Permutation: closed-form one-way binomial LR statistic (verified identical to the GLM deviance difference), 5000 habitat-label shuffles, p = (1+{perm>=obs})/(5000+1) -> resolution floor 0.0002.

## Outputs
- table1_descriptive_by_habitat.csv - both layers, Wilson CIs, mean-of-plot-ratios, status flag.
- table2_glm_coefficients.csv - logit coefficients, 95% CIs, ORs, separation notes.
- table3_pairwise_holm.csv - 15 eligible contrasts (Fisher + Holm).
- table4_sensitivity.csv - presence response, quasi-binomial, collapsed semi-natural, covariate-adjusted robustness runs (urban 1000m/50m, cropland 1000m).
- table5_temporal_context.csv - background temporal trend.
- table6_pathway_composition.csv - gard/unint/agfo shares and dominant pathway per habitat.
- table7_uncond_pairwise_holm.csv - 45 unconditional-layer contrasts, Holm.
- table8_jackknife_drop1plot.csv - drop-one-plot stability of key contrasts.
- figure1_forest_ascii.txt - ASCII forest plot, conditional layer, Wilson CIs.
- summary.json - all headline statistics.
- hypothesis.md - final hypothesis paragraph.

## Key diagnostics
- Dispersion: deviance/df = 1.204, Pearson/df = 0.982 -> no overdispersion; quasi-binomial scale 0.541, max habitat-SE inflation 1.21x, conclusions unchanged.
- Covariate robustness: adding elevation + log(distance.road) + urban.2009.1000m (or urban.2009.50m, or cropland.2009.1000m) leaves habitat significant (LR ~55.3-55.8, p ~9e-9), max |log OR shift| 0.73, max SE ratio 1.24. Habitat is NOT separable from the urbanisation gradient in these data.
- Collapsed semi-natural run (sensitivity only, not used in the hypothesis): SemiNatural 54.8% conditional, habitat LR(4 df) = 36.7, p = 2e-7 - direction consistent with the 10-level model.
- Dominant species: top-3 gardening species (Robinia pseudoacacia 20, Dysphania ambrosioides 15, Oxalis debilis 12 plots) = 28.8% of gardening records - below the 30% alert level, but close to it; note the single most common non-native overall (Erigeron sumatrensis, 53 plots) is unintentional.
- Jackknife (drop one plot, 191 refits): Wetlands-Croplands OR 4.97-6.99, Coastal-Croplands 4.40-5.78, Wetlands-Urban 2.66-3.74, all p<0.05 in every refit.

## Known data caveats
- 441/632 plots (69.8%) have zero non-native records: the conditional layer is conditional on a plot being invaded (n = 191).
- 4 habitats hold <=8 records total -> descriptive only, direction not interpreted.
- Same species recurs across plots, so binomial trials are not fully independent (no species x plot matrix to fix this); addressed with presence-response and jackknife checks.
- 481 records in the plot matrix vs 472 (452 non-duplicated) in the species table - unexplained 2-6% mismatch; species table used for magnitude only.
- No survey-effort variable -> detection bias cannot be controlled; land-cover columns are fractions 0-1 despite "percentage" in the metadata; coordinates are UTM metres.
